      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Regarding fees, ETFs generally have lower expense ratios because many are passively managed, which keeps operating costs down. Mutual funds can have higher operational costs, particularly actively managed ones, which are reflected in their expense ratios or sales loads. Clients should watch out for \"loads\" in mutual funds (front-end or back-end sales fees) and potential trading commissions if they manually buy/sell ETFs through a broker.",
      "source": "target",
